<p>President Trump is holding a Saturday meeting with a group of Latin American leaders at his Miami-area golf club, according to preview coverage. Reports describe a gathering built around shared priorities—countering drug trafficking, managing migration pressures, and tackling broader security concerns across the region. Several outlets also place the summit in a wider geopolitical context. China has spent years deepening economic and political ties across Latin America, and the meeting is framed as part of a US push to strengthen partnerships with ideologically aligned governments as a counterweight to Beijing’s influence.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Who’s expected: Reports previewing the summit say Argentina’s President Javier Milei, Ecuador’s President Daniel Noboa, and El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele are among the expected attendees.</li><li>A security template: Firstpost says Bukele’s security crackdown in El Salvador has become a model for many in the region as governments grapple with violent criminal groups.</li><li>What it’s called: Firstpost describes the gathering as the “Shield of the Americas” meeting.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: The administration is presenting the meeting as a chance to shift attention—at least temporarily—toward the Western Hemisphere and closer coordination with regional leaders. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/07/g-s1-112852/trump-americas-summit'>NPR</a>)</li><li>BBC analysis: The BBC frames the summit as part of a US push to counter China’s growing influence in Latin America by working with ideologically aligned leaders. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yvw0zwpd5o'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Regional governments: Coverage highlights shared worries about the power of drug cartels and their cross-border fallout, which helps explain why security cooperation is taking center stage. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-convenes-latin-american-leaders-to-curb-crime-immigration'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/07/g-s1-112852/trump-americas-summit'>Trump looks to turn attention to Western Hemisphere at Americas summit</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yvw0zwpd5o'>China spent years building ties in Latin America. Can Trump make room for the US?</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/shield-of-the-americas-trump-to-meet-latin-american-leaders-discuss-drug-trafficking-and-immigration-13987042.html'>&#x27;Shield of the Americas&#x27;: Trump to meet Latin American leaders, discuss drug trafficking and immigration</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-convenes-latin-american-leaders-to-curb-crime-immigration'>Trump convenes Latin American leaders to curb crime, immigration</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>